Mix.Tasks.Compile.All: keep the code paths of Elixir in a project with language: :erlang

Before a compile, Mix removes each code path that is not of an
application of the project. A project with language: :erlang does not
list the applications of Elixir, so Mix removed the code paths of
Elixir and of Mix itself. Each module of Elixir that was not loaded yet
then gave undef, for example Path.Wildcard.list_dir/1 at the first
Path.wildcard/2 of the compile.

Keep the code paths of the applications of Elixir. In a usual install,
the code path of Elixir has the form ELIXIR/bin/../lib, which
Code.delete_paths/1 does not find, so nothing changes there.

--- a/lib/mix/lib/mix/tasks/compile.all.ex
+++ b/lib/mix/lib/mix/tasks/compile.all.ex
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@
     current_paths = :code.get_path()
 
     if Keyword.get(config, :prune_code_paths, true) and "--no-prune-code-paths" not in args do
-      Code.delete_paths(current_paths -- loaded_paths)
+      Code.delete_paths(current_paths -- (loaded_paths ++ elixir_paths()))
     end
 
     Code.prepend_paths(loaded_paths -- current_paths, cache: true)
@@ -97,6 +97,19 @@
     {status, diagnostics}
   end
 
+  # The code paths of the applications of Elixir stay. Mix itself runs from
+  # them, also for a project with language: :erlang, which does not list
+  # them. In a usual install, the code path has the form ELIXIR/bin/../lib,
+  # which Code.delete_paths/1 does not find, so these paths stayed already.
+  # In one file with OTP and Elixir (beam.com), they are in the lib
+  # directory of OTP, and Mix removed them.
+  defp elixir_paths do
+    for app <- [:elixir, :eex, :ex_unit, :iex, :logger, :mix],
+        dir <- [:code.lib_dir(app)],
+        is_list(dir),
+        do: :filename.join(dir, ~c"ebin")
+  end
+
   @doc """
   Returns all apps that should be available at compile time.
   """
